{title: Be Thou My Vision}
{author: Carlton Young, Eleanor Hull, Keith Landis, Mary Byrne }

{key: D}
{time: 3/4}

{comment: Verse 1}
[D]Be Thou my vision, O Lord of my heart
[A]Naught be all else to me, [G]save that Thou [A]art
[G]Thou my best [D/F#]thought, by [Bm]day or by [G]night 
[D]Waking or [Bm]sleeping, Thy [G]presence my [D]light
 
{comment: Verse 2}
[D]Be Thou my vision and Thou my true word
[A]I ever with Thee and [G]Thou with me, [A]Lord
[G]Thou my great [D/F#]Father, and [Bm]I Thy true [G]son
[D]Thou in me [Bm]dwelling and [G]I with [A]Thee [D]one

{comment: Verse 3}
[D]Be thou my battle shield, sword for the fight; 
[A]Be thou my dignity, [G]Thou my delight
[G]Thou my soul’s [D/F#]shelter, [Bm]Thou my strong [G]tide;  
[D]Raise Thou me [Bm]heavenward, O [G]pow’r of [A]my [D]might

{comment: Verse 4}
[D]Riches I heed not, not man’s empty praise; 
[A]Thou mine inheritance, [G]now and al[A]ways
[G]Thou and Thou [D/F#]only, [Bm]first in my [G]heart; 
[D]High King of [Bm]heaven, my [A]treasure [G]Thou [D]art

[D]High King of heaven, my victory won. 
[G]May I reach heaven’s joys, [G]O bright heav’n’s [A]son
[G]Heart of my [D/F#]own heart, what[Bm]ever be[G]falll; 
[D]Still be my [Bm]vision, O [G]ruler [A]of [D]all

